{
 "assembly_notes": "Two structural slots plus the caster multiplicity. frame_style publishes the boom pivot at the mast top, N caster stations along whatever leg run it actually built, and a ram foot bracket clear of the mast; boom_style consumes only the pivot and republishes a hook seat on whichever section carries the tip. hook_style hangs on whichever section carries the tip. All 5 x 3 x 2 = 30 combinations x 2 caster counts build with no compatibility gate. Every pin is a stub pair outboard of the eye it carries, every cylinder and boom section is a real hollow shell with a 1.6 mm sliding fit, and the telescoping chain tracks its parent's length so each stage stays engaged in the one it slides in. The swing-out outriggers are their own slot: their brackets bolt to the outer face of whichever leg run the base candidate built (outboard of braces, ballast straps, fold lugs and mast struts), so any base can carry them and the caster stations are untouched.",
